{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwUqk1CWKXNBNTV9gMr6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't checked how the dashboard panels render, and the rule's status was still \"pending\" when it was created.\n\n**Data:** The data view `kibana_sample_data_logs` uses `timestamp` as its time field. The fields I used were:\n- `response.keyword` (the HTTP status code)\n- `extension.keyword`\n- `bytes`\n\nOther fields include `clientip`, `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `host`, `url`, `agent` and `referer`.\n\n**Dashboard \"EFF-9b464f45 Web logs overview\"** (id `eff-9b464f45-web-logs-overview-b032618e5316`, 4 panels):\n- Total requests, as a single number.\n- Requests over time, as a line chart.\n- Responses by status code, as a pie chart.\n- Average bytes by file extension, as a bar chart.\n\nIt's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-9b464f45-web-logs-overview-b032618e5316.\n\n**Rule \"EFF-9b464f45 5xx spike\"** (id `806ab100-f0d6-44fd-96d9-238dba4fecf1`):\n- It is an Elasticsearch query rule that runs every minute.\n- It looks at the last 5 minutes of `kibana_sample_data_logs`, counts documents where `response.keyword` matches `5*`, and fires when the count is above 10.\n- I didn't attach any notification action, so firing only creates an alert in Kibana.\n\nThe sample data's timestamps may not be current. If so, the rule's 5-minute window may not match any documents, so it may never fire."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1272,"cache_read_input_tokens":19907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1272},"output_tokens":561,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"se